From cf988e5a96b54a5b74b733e38dde42dd9f3d55c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mateus Seiboth <mateusseiboth12@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 09:21:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] lisa port: Goodix touch clock HWCG fix, device packaging,
 capybara/6BOT branding

- drivers/input/hakios.goodix.c: the QUP1 master/slave AHB branches are HWCG
  (hwcg_bit=1 in gcc-sc7280), so their CBCR keeps CLK_OFF set while idle and it
  never clears; clear HWCG to free-run them and wait only on the serial-engine
  branch. Replaces the earlier branch-enable attempt that left S_AHB at
  0x8000000a.
- tools/mkubootimg.py: per-device prebuilt/bootimg.args (e.g. --base 0x0 for lisa's ABL).
- userland/build.sh: copy (not hard-link) the dyld shared cache into the image;
  keep sysroot only with KEEP_SYSROOT.
- xnuloader/loader.c: capybara boot logo and the 6BOT banner.
- devices/lisa: the lisa device repository (submodule), configs and boot-args.
