From f8a0aa0d4267b83139f6af7a45933afa3664078d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mateus Seiboth <mateusseiboth12@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:15:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] goodix: support the gt9897 (Goodix Berlin variant A),
 working on lisa

lisa's touch controller is a gt9897 ("variant A"), not the gt9916 ("variant D")
the driver was written for, and the two differ in three ways that together left the
chip unreadable ("no valid firmware version" / "no goodix touch screen"):

- register addresses: fw-version 0x1000C and ic-info 0x10068 on variant A, 0x10014
  and 0x10070 on D. Reading D's 0x10014 landed eight bytes into the struct.
- SPI read framing: four dummy bytes (a nine-byte prefix) on A, three (eight) on D.
- the mainline dev_confirm handshake (write 8x0xAA to the boot-option register and
  read it back) before the first read, which both confirms the link and, being a
  known pattern, shows the read is aligned.

Also: bring_up never released the chip from reset before probing (power_on holds
RESET low); call touch_reset() first. boot-arg touch_goodix_a=1 selects variant A;
the default stays variant D for the reference phone. The FIFO interface is disabled
on lisa's serial engine (GSI-only), so the driver bit-bangs the pins, which the
handshake proved reliable. Confirmed on hardware: chip "BERLIN", firmware "9897T",
"touch screen ready".
---
 configs/boot-args.lst         |  2 +
 configs/symbols.tsv           |  2 +
 docs/boot-args.md             |  6 ++-
 drivers/input/hakios.goodix.c | 88 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 4 files changed, 86 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/configs/boot-args.lst b/configs/boot-args.lst
index bd70726..683c547 100644
